-- title:
--   The capacity procedure returns the next power of two
-- statement:
--   Fix a program containing the capacity procedure, resource limits, a call depth, and initial memory $\mu$. Let $p\in\mathbb N$ be positive, and suppose $2p+1$ fits within the word-magnitude limit. Put $c=\operatorname{clog}_2(p)$, the least natural number with $p\le2^c$. The procedure called on $p$ returns
--
--   $$r=2^c,\qquad\mu'=\mu,\qquad\text{cost}\le12c+10.$$
--
--   This computes the polynomial array capacity directly in the machine model and preserves memory.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightCapacity.lean#L27-L58

